    <decisions>
        <name>Parent_Needs_Reopening</name>
        <label>Parent Already Approved or Pending?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Not Yet Submitted - No Action</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Needs_Reopening</name>
            <conditionLogic>1 OR 2</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Appraisal.AF_ApprovalStatus__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Approved</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Appraisal.AF_ApprovalStatus__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Pending</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Queue_Group</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Approved or Pending</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Fixes defect RS04-08 (report defect #5): a vehicle added to a trade-in AFTER it was already Approved (or while a sibling item is still Pending) previously landed in a dead end - the Used Car Team had lost queue ownership (reassigned back to the rep on approval) so they couldn&apos;t value it, the rep isn&apos;t allowed to value it either (AppraisalItem.InitialValue is Used-Car-Team-only by design), and nothing reacted to the new item at all. The parent Appraisal kept reading Approved while silently containing an unevaluated vehicle.

This flow fires whenever a new AppraisalItem is created and automatically reopens its parent Appraisal for evaluation - same reassign-to-queue mechanism AF_FL_Appraisal_SubmitForEvaluation uses (Owner -&gt; AF_Q_UsedCarTeam queue, Status=&apos;Visit Scheduled&apos;, AF_ApprovalStatus__c=Pending, AF_TradeInOutcome__c=&apos;In Progress&apos;) plus a queue notification, so the new vehicle is guaranteed to reach someone who can value it instead of requiring the rep to notice and manually press Submit for Evaluation again on a record that already reads Approved (undiscoverable in practice). Only fires when the parent is Approved or Pending - a first-time item added to a brand-new (blank AF_ApprovalStatus__c) Appraisal is the normal creation path already handled by the rep&apos;s own Submit for Evaluation action, so no action is needed there.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
